<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mengistu Haile Mariam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mengistu Haile Mariam was an Ethiopian army officer who rose to lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a>, the military council that overthrew Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> in 1974. The coup ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> and the Solomonic monarchy. Mengistu ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> as a Marxist dictator until 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam.jpg" alt="Mengistu Haile Mariam" width="300" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mengistu_Haile_Mariam_official_portrait,_1977-1978.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
